;; repr/scheme's negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a), "As built: GT9's controls"): each is a crossed pair of two files of
;; a corpus (keys as bin/repr-scheme check names them: CORPUS/PATH, probe/NAME), both passing, the SUBJECT judged by the family's own
;; judge against the REFERENCE, which must fail. :levels names the families that run it:
;;   :check      bin/repr-scheme check (arbace.repr.scheme.check/compare-file): Arbace's reading and writing of the subject's text against
;;               the reference's Chez dump (tree, offsets, `write`, errors); equal is a control that passed
;;   :roundtrip  bin/repr-scheme roundtrip (arbace.repr.scheme/roundtrip-judge): the subject's stages (the :full print, the forms read
;;               again, the layout's forms, the layout's idempotence) against the reference's text and stages; every one of the four
;;               levels must fail, one that holds is a control that passed
;; A control that passes fails the run; one whose files the run lacks (a corpus not fetched, --quick's probes) is left. No control
;; is a file of the corpora, the known file (check-known.edn) or the counts. Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id "_control/enums-vs-lists" :subject "racket-r6rs/r6rs/enums.sls" :reference "racket-r6rs/r6rs/lists.sls" :levels [:check :roundtrip]
  :why "two library files of the R6RS tests, other data, other offsets, other text; neither is in check-known.edn"}]
